  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1245 AM CDT Wed Apr 22 2026\n\nWe will transition into nearly summer-like conditions by \nThursday, and keep them through early next week. On Thursday, \nalthough an upper level trough will be moving across the central \nand northern CONUS, we will be under zonal flow. In the lower \nlevels, 850mb temperatures will be close to 10 degrees Celsius \nwarmer than we have seen lately. This warming, coupled with \nafternoon sunshine, and south to southwesterly surface winds will \nallow for temperatures to warm into the mid 80s to lower 90s. \nZonal to west/southwest flow aloft will continue through the first\nhalf of next week, with weak disturbances moving through. The low\nlevel thermal ridge will be maintained, keeping our afternoon \nhighs 5 to 10 degrees above the normal highs around 80 degrees. \nAlthough there will be shortwave disturbances moving through, \nprecipitation chances remain less than 20% through most of the \nforecast with the next low chance for showers and thunderstorms \nnot expected until next Tuesday into Wednesday when a weak cold \nfront may move into the area.",
